WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.140
Part three of three: from tests to a safe decision. Part two
took one issue through triage, approval, and trusted QA tests.

2
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.188
Blue means live. Purple means a recorded real run. Red means
scripted, with no model.

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:26.088
Teal means a decision that the AI Simulated User takes at the
owner's request. Grey means that waiting time is cut inside one
page.

4
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:37.124
The AI Simulated User operates Factory at the owner's request.
No human appears in this demo, and every review is an agent
review.

5
00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:45.237
The coding run works inside its approved budget.

6
00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:51.953
Factory checks the build, the tests, the hidden QA tests, and
the scope.

7
00:00:53.233 --> 00:00:56.569
The Judge scores four dimensions, from one to five.

8
00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:02.785
If every score is at least four, and there is no finding, the
loop is done.

9
00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:08.589
Then the loop is ready for review. It never approves.

10
00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:14.485
Otherwise a revision starts from the same candidate, with the
findings.

11
00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:24.137
Limits: a minimum score, a maximum number of revisions, cost
caps, and one retry if the Judge answer breaks the format.

12
00:01:24.733 --> 00:01:30.973
Then the review. Tests are the evidence for requirements with
tests. Human checks need their own evidence.

13
00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:38.277
With the evidence, the review approves with a reason. The draft
pull request and CI follow.

14
00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:44.441
Without it, notes are saved, the review stays pending, and
nothing is published.

15
00:01:47.741 --> 00:01:51.197
Now the first coding attempt, from the approved work item.

16
00:01:55.441 --> 00:01:58.489
The AI Simulated User opens Start run.

17
00:02:01.341 --> 00:02:05.805
The form shows the approved request, the allowed paths, and the
checks.

18
00:02:08.041 --> 00:02:13.633
The approved QA tests are a protected check. The coding agent
gets only the interface note.

19
00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:28.461
The card shows the exact attempt, the model, and the money
limit: fifty cents for all rounds.

20
00:02:31.341 --> 00:02:33.957
The AI Simulated User confirms it.

21
00:02:34.257 --> 00:02:38.937
The run starts. The status, the checks, and the progress are at
the top.

22
00:02:41.341 --> 00:02:44.461
Live activity shows each step of the agent.

23
00:02:49.641 --> 00:02:54.705
The agent changes the code, and Factory verifies it. The waiting
time is cut.

24
00:02:58.941 --> 00:03:04.725
The run ended and is verified. All thirty-five checks pass, and
the scope is respected.

25
00:03:10.141 --> 00:03:16.453
Each requirement shows the result of the check that covers it.
Two are human checks, and wait for review.

26
00:03:21.041 --> 00:03:24.305
It cost three cents, with sixteen requests.

27
00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:31.456
Next, the Judge loop, on the run page.

28
00:03:34.208 --> 00:03:39.896
The Judge scores the candidate. A low score starts a revision
inside the approved limits.

29
00:03:47.208 --> 00:03:54.000
The dialog shows the limits: minimum score four, at most two
revisions, and a total limit of three dollars.

30
00:03:55.308 --> 00:04:00.372
Factory shows the settings digest. The loop runs only inside
these limits.

31
00:04:08.308 --> 00:04:11.620
The AI Simulated User approves the bounded loop.

32
00:04:12.008 --> 00:04:16.712
The loop starts. The Judge scores the first candidate on four
dimensions.

33
00:04:18.808 --> 00:04:20.560
The waiting time is cut here.

34
00:04:27.508 --> 00:04:36.820
The loop is ready for review after round one. The scores are
five, five, five, and five. All meet the minimum, so no revision
was needed.

35
00:04:42.008 --> 00:04:46.952
The loop never approves or merges. The Judge cost six tenths of
a cent.

36
00:04:50.252 --> 00:04:55.748
The review of the final candidate. The AI Simulated User opens
it from the run page.

37
00:05:03.252 --> 00:05:07.308
The review page lists the requirements, each with its check
result.

38
00:05:08.152 --> 00:05:11.968
It is an agent review, and it is not independent of the Judge.

39
00:05:29.152 --> 00:05:34.744
A passing check is the evidence for its requirement. A human
check needs its own verification.

40
00:05:39.052 --> 00:05:43.660
The AI Simulated User marks the requirements that have evidence
as met.

41
00:05:59.352 --> 00:06:12.048
Requirements five and six are human checks. The run's
screenshots show the Open and All lists, and one completion.
They do not show the Overdue list with an open task, or an
update without a reload.

42
00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:31.072
The AI Simulated User saves a note for each, and leaves the
review pending.

43
00:06:33.152 --> 00:06:38.552
The review is pending. The AI Simulated User did not approve
without the evidence.

44
00:06:44.719 --> 00:06:50.095
Decision and publication. The review is pending, so there is
nothing to approve.

45
00:06:52.519 --> 00:06:56.095
No decision is recorded, so there is nothing to publish.

46
00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:04.643
The saved notes are on the review. Factory needs the evidence
first.

47
00:07:16.019 --> 00:07:20.771
The run has no pull request. Nothing was published. The demo
stops here.

48
00:07:24.286 --> 00:07:28.942
The evidence of part three: the run, the Judge loop, and the
review.

49
00:07:30.286 --> 00:07:36.334
The total model cost of the whole recording was twenty-two
cents, of the approved four dollars seventy.

50
00:07:37.786 --> 00:07:46.762
The Judge loop needed no revision. Chapters thirteen and
fourteen ended with a pending review. Nothing was published, and
there is no finished feature.

51
00:07:47.886 --> 00:07:53.454
The review is an agent review. The demo does not show that
Factory saves engineering time.

52
00:07:54.786 --> 00:07:58.986
The AI Simulated User was played by Claude Code at the owner's
request.
